From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:05:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 052/342] mmc: verify fast modes with multi-block reads, fall
 back on errors

After the update to SD high speed, an ODROID-C2 booting from its
microSD no longer came up; its card had passed only three single-block
test reads at 50 MHz. Fast modes are now harder to get into and easier
to leave:

- meson_gx_mmc keeps an SD card above 25 MHz only if three 128-block
  reads at the new clock pass (as for eMMC DDR52). The device interface's
  set_clock() now returns the outcome, so mmc_disk logs the speed used.
- A transfer that fails in a fast mode is retried once at a safe speed,
  which stays: SD at 25 MHz, eMMC DDR at 26 MHz.
- "sd_high_speed false" in the meson_gx_mmc driver settings keeps SD
  cards at 25 MHz, like "emmc_ddr false" for DDR52.

Tested on the ODROID-C2: its SD card passes at 50 MHz; with the setting
it stays at 25 MHz (11.7 MB/s); eMMC DDR52 unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
